 ### Fast Linear Assignment Sorting (Fast LAS)
-An adaptation of Linear Assignment Sorting (LAS) that outperforms other sorting methods in speed and quality for non-parallel computations by swapping all (or several) vectors simultaneously using a continuously filtered map [S1]. Designed to handle millions of items (e.g., Gaussians) where standard grid-sorting algorithms are inadequate [S1]. Enables continuous sorting of Gaussian data during training [S1]. When to choose: Not given in the sources. Link: Not given in the sources.
